	(text "scales 0-3.3V -> -0.2-3.3V.\noffset: Vo1 = -V_REF(6.04/100) = -0.2\nCV: Vo2 = V_Ci(1 + 6.04/100)\n=> Vo = Vo1 + Vo2 = V_Ci(1 + 6.04/100) - 3.3(6.04/100)\n\nsallen key filter that forms 2nd order LP:\nf0 = 1/2piRC = 339Hz, with the 2nd order Q, fc (-3dB) = 224Hz.\n\ntogether these circuits form the full CV buffer\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.686 31.75 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "19416794-8a69-4ccd-bda3-5d4c17f334c1")
	)
	(text "temp compensation:\nThe VCA has this gain factor: -33mV/dB at 25C. so for every 33mV the control voltage\ndecreases, the audio gets 1dB louder.\n\nPROBLEM:\nthe VCAs CV scales by 0.33%/degC. So if 0.66V gives -20dB at 25C,\nif the temp rises to 35C, the new gain factor is\n   -33mv/dB * (1 + 10degC * 0.33%)\n      = 1.033*-33\n      = -34.089mV/dB\n\nSo with the same 0.66V CV, instead of -20dB, you get, 0.66/-34.089mV = -19.36dB :(\n\nSOLUTION:\n(From datasheet LM334):\nV_(R_SET) = 227uV/degK * T (temp in K)\ndV_(R_SET) = 227uV/degC\n=> @25C = 298K, V_(R_SET)\n    = 67.6mV @25C = I_SET * R_SET\n\nI_SET = V_(R_SET) / R_SET, I_OUT = I_SET\n\n@ the output node (-):\nV_REF = I_TOTAL * R_L. ohms law\nI_TOTAL = I_OUT + I_BIAS. KCL\nNominally, I_BIAS = ~I_OUT/18 (datasheet)\n=> I_TOTAL = I_OUT + I_BIAS\n    = ~1.06I_OUT\n\nI_SET = V_R / R_SET\n\n=> V_REF = 1.06 * I_OUT * R_L\n    = 1.06(V_(R_SET) / R_SET) * R_L\n    = 1.06(R_L * 227uV/C * T) / R_SET\n\nSince we want V_REF = 3.3V, set R_L = 10k => I_TOTAL = 330uA\nThe nominal temperature (where TI measured all these) is 25C = 298K.\n\n=> V_REF = 1.06(10k * 227u * 298) / R_SET = 3.3V\n=> R_SET = 1.06 * 10k * 227u * 298 / 3.3 = 217 ohms.\n"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 245.618 69.85 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "23536633-37a2-4be5-b02f-f01c02dfa62f")
	)
